# Codex Rules — Git and filesystem safety for RivalLens
#
# Codex Rules are experimental and the schema is evolving. The authoritative
# enforcement lives in .codex/hooks/safety_guard.py, which blocks the
# following operations at the PreToolUse stage:
#
#   git add .
#   git add -A
#   git add --all
#   git reset --hard
#   git clean -f*  (e.g. -fd, -fdx)
#   rm -r*f*       (recursive forced delete)
#   Remove-Item ... -Recurse -Force
#
# Rationale:
#   - Broad staging hides unrelated dirty files in a monorepo.
#   - Destructive resets/cleans can lose uncommitted local work.
#   - Recursive forced deletes can wipe data/ or .env files unintentionally.
#
# If you need any of the above, ask the user for explicit approval first
# and pass concrete paths rather than wildcards.
